.Sh HISTORY
The hash algorithm used in the
.Sy -subject_hash
and
.Sy -issuer_hash
options before OpenSSL 1.0.0 was based on the deprecated MD5 algorithm
and the encoding of the distinguished name.
In OpenSSL 1.0.0 and later it is based on a canonical version of the DN
using SHA1. This means that any directories using the old form must have
their links rebuilt using
.Xr openssl-rehash 1
or similar.
.Pp
The
.Sy -signkey
option has been renamed to
.Sy -key
in OpenSSL 3.0, keeping the old name as an alias.
.Pp
The
.Sy -engine
option was deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
The
.Sy -C
option was removed in OpenSSL 3.0.
.Pp
Since OpenSSL 3.2, generated certificates bear X.509 version 3, and key
identifier extensions are included by default.
